    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling core, anchored by **Christian Yelich** (75.84) and **Yordan Alvarez** (74.97). **Christian Yelich** is our premier play, leveraging a massive +13% platoon advantage against Andrew Painter; despite a league-average catcher arm, his spot atop the order makes him a primary source for both runs and stolen bases. Similarly, **Junior Caminero** (74.72) benefits from the day's softest matchup against Sam Aldegheri (5.47 xERA), where a high-velocity offensive environment should facilitate significant production. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (71.57) rounds out our elite tier, as his aggressive base-running and high-volume spot at the top of the order provide a stable floor despite a slight park penalty.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the coaching staff involved **Colt Keith** (57.53), who sat on the bubble as our top bench option. While **Colt Keith** carries an attractive platoon edge, the optimizer ultimately favored the specific lineup construction and superior scoring output of **Caleb Durbin** (58.26), whose matchup against Jack Leiter offers a unique opportunity for stolen bases due to the pitcher's slow delivery to the plate. Elsewhere, we are bracing for volatility from **Trea Turner** (50.39) and **Kyle Schwarber** (49.64); both face the significant hurdle of Jacob Misiorowski, whose elite stuff mandates a cautionary outlook. While **Carson Benge** (60.24) faces the daunting Spencer Strider, the combination of favorable wind conditions and his high-leverage leadoff spot maintains his status as a recommended start over the bench reserves.",
